 u1 chip will be a huge part of the  apple ecosystem  and he expects most apple products in  the future to come with one of these  chips  that has already been in the iphone  since last year's 11 pro  now moving on to december nikkei  reported that we should be getting a new  apple tv  sometime in 2021 but they didn't mention  any specific  dates then later that month bloomberg  once again confirmed that we're still  getting a new apple tv  with an updated remote in 2021 and they  mentioned that it's gonna have a  stronger  gaming focus saying that there's going  to be a big leap  in terms of hardware and software to  remain  competitive in the long term this goes  to show that apple is planning something  big for this new apple tv pushing into  the gaming segment and that's probably  why it's taking so long  and we can for sure expect a very  powerful chip  like the a14x and now getting into the  most  recent groundbreaking leaks left a dream  posted some images of the current apple  tv remote  with a tagline saying it's time to  change  once again confirming that a new remote  will be coming with the new tv  so just by looking at all of those leaks  and rumors  we should be getting extremely excited  however  there is still some very bad news that  we gotta cover  so let's get into that many people were  hoping for a release date  this march but we just got a major new  rumor to date from  the verifier apparently this new apple  tv  is actually coming later this year in  the fourth quarter  which means between october and the end  of the year they say that apple will be  hosting a special  apple tv plus event where they will  reveal some new movie and show content  as well as the new tv os 15 features  like a major software design  refresh a better app store ui a new kids  mode with better parental controls and  channel subscription bundles  so based on those most recent rumors  it's a bit sad to see that the apple tv  could be launching way later than we  expected  but there could actually be a very good  reason for it  the verifier claim that apple is in  advanced talks  with major and well-known gaming  companies  in order to offer their games outside of  the xbox  playstation and pc consoles this  basically means that apple is trying to  get  aaa game developers to bring their games  to the apple tv  and potentially more apple products so  if we can get some awesome  aaa titles to the apple tv it'll greatly  help apples push into the gaming market  so it's going to be worth spending tons  of cash just on game development and  getting  ports over to the apple tv this is  extremely exciting because it opens up  the possibility  of cross-platform play which is  basically required  if you want to have a competitive gaming  console these days  they also mentioned that there would be  a new apple remote as well as an actual  dedicated gaming controller which will  probably be an  optional add-on we actually saw various  leaks and rumors about a dedicated  controller coming  and it falls in line with apple's recent  software updates  which added major controller features  like button remapping  better haptics and rumble showing that  apple was planning to get big into  gaming very soon now with all of those  leaks and rumors out of the way let me  speculate on what apple is planning to  do  and how they can pull off the apple tv  launch first off if they truly are  planning to delay the release date  until the end of the year this points to  apple waiting on the rumored  aaa games to be ready before launching  the apple tv  this shows that they want all of their  cards to fall into place  before making the big launch and this  gives them  more time to make deals with major game  developers as well  if apple does reveal a new gaming  controller  for the apple tv there's a good chance  that they will open up tv os  to natively play ipad games as well  since the ipad now has really good  controller support  and apple did add cross